# Skill: Masters Programme Page Content Improvement

This skill encodes the client's standing content rules for all masters
program-detail pages (Rushford MBA/MSc, GAU MBA/EMBA/MSc, UCA, UWS,
Wolverhampton). Follow every section when writing, editing, or reviewing
these files.

## 1. Brand voice — we ARE Maverick Business Academy London

We represent Maverick Business Academy London. We never speak as a web page.

Banned (rewrite on sight):
- "on this page", "this page carries/prints/shows/answers", "listed on the page", "the page names"

Rewrites (rotate so files do not repeat the same sentence):
- "this page carries no fixed number" → "Maverick Business Academy London shares no fixed number up front"
- "no fixed figure sits on this page" → "no fixed figure is published up front"
- "named on this page" → "named by our admissions team and on your certificate"
- "printed on this page" → "confirmed in writing before you pay"
- General rule: replace the page as subject with "we", "our admissions team", or "Maverick Business Academy London".

## 2. Language — English-US only

Client requirement: US spelling everywhere. Convert UK forms on sight:

| UK (wrong) | US (required) |
|---|---|
| programme / programmes | program / programs |
| specialisation | specialization |
| organisation | organization |
| analyse / analyses / analysing | analyze / analyzes / analyzing |
| centre | center |
| labour, favour, colour, behaviour, rigour | labor, favor, color, behavior, rigor |
| recognise / recognised / recognising | recognize / recognized / recognizing |
| enrol / enrolment / enrolled | enroll / enrollment / enrolled |
| instalment | installment |
| licence (noun) | license |

Keep: "analysis" (valid in both), proper names exactly as the owner writes
them (e.g., World Health Organization).

## 3. Numbers — figures, not words

Use digits for every quantity: statistics, money, percentages, credits,
months, years, counts, ages, ratios.

| Wrong | Right |
|---|---|
| Nineteen and a half million visitors | 19.5 million visitors |
| eighty percent occupancy | 80% occupancy |
| Sixty ECTS in twelve months | 60 ECTS in 12 months |
| fifteen courses of four ECTS | 15 courses of 4 ECTS |
| over eighteen months | over 18 months |
| the twenty-first century | the 21st century |
| nine in ten employers | 9 in 10 employers |

Exceptions: a number that opens a sentence (restructure instead of spelling
it out), and non-quantitative idioms ("one of the largest", "a year").
Never mix formats in one file: if "16 months" is digits, every other
duration must be digits too.

## 4. Banned AI patterns (client red-flag list)

Never in client-facing copy:
- Em/en dashes (— or –). Use commas, colons, periods, or "to".
- Jargon tells: delve, align, tapestry, seamless, leverage, utilize, empower, unlock, embark, robust, comprehensive, holistic, foster, elevate, tailored, ensure, cutting-edge, landscape, game-changer, pivotal, crucial, paramount, myriad, plethora, showcase, underscore, realm, dynamic world, ever-evolving, fast-paced.
- Formula frames: "X isn't just Y", "In today's...", "In an era...", "At its core", "stands as", "serves as", "Whether you...", "more than just", "In conclusion".
- Mononymous "Conclusion" headers; use sentence-case headers.
- 3 clipped sentences in a row; vary sentence length deliberately.
- Emoji anywhere.
- Personification max once per page.

## 5. Claims — official sources only

A claim stays ONLY if it traces to an official website: the awarding
university, a government ministry/regulator (MoHESR, MOHRE, KHDA, DET,
Central Bank, Dubai Media Office, ADIO), a law, or an official
accreditation body (EduQua, IACBE, QS, YÖDAK/YÖK, Ofqual, QAA).

Remove or rewrite qualitative (no figures) when sourced from: private
research firms (Mordor, MarkNtel, Ken Research, IMARC), recruitment/data
firms (Taggd, Labeeb), trade publications (Logistics Middle East), venture
data (MAGNiTT, Wamda, GrowthList), blogs and aggregators. Never invent a
replacement figure. The client-approved AED 16,000 to 40,000 masters fee
band stays. Never print a salary promise.

## 6. Human style (v5 maximally-human pattern)

- Vary rhythm: mix long winding sentences with short ones; never 3 clipped in a row.
- Use parenthetical asides and concrete, checkable detail.
- Keep the "Honest take:" marker where the template has one; it states limits plainly.
- Uneven benefit cards (different lengths) beat uniform cards.
- Real role names, real institutions, dated policies beat generic promises.
- Simple English. No corporate polish. Target AI-detector result under 10 to 20%.

## 7. Structure and tooling

- Keep the field structure: `# title` → metadata block → `## SEO` → numbered
  sections (HERO, AT A GLANCE, OVERVIEW, WHY CHOOSE, LEARNING OUTCOMES,
  CAREERS, STRUCTURE, support, GCC context, FEES) → `## BUILD NOTES`.
- BUILD NOTES is internal: sources, flags, dated change lines. It never
  appears in DOCX output.
- After editing md, regenerate DOCX:
  `python3 landing-page/program-detail/md_to_docx.py <files>`
- Before finishing, sweep for: em/en dashes = 0, banned words = 0,
  "this page" = 0 in body, UK spellings = 0, words-for-numbers = 0.

## 8. Grammarly (if available)

Use only as a grammar/spelling/punctuation checker (US dictionary).
Reject its voice, clarity, and formality rewrites; they push text toward
generic AI-flavoured English and raise detector scores. After accepting
fixes, re-run the banned-pattern sweep in section 4.
